{title: Paper Lanterns}
{artist: The Placeholders}
{album: Example Songs}
{key: G}

# An original example song so the app has something to show.

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Paper lanterns [D]on the line
[Em]Swaying slow in the [C]evening wind
[G]Someone hums an [D]old refrain
[C]Down the street and [D]back again
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Light them up, [G]light them up
[Em]Hold the night a [D]little longer
[C]Light them up, [G]light them up
[D]Every flame a [G]little stronger
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Chalk lines on the [D]harbour wall
[Em]Names we wrote when [C]we were small
[G]Rain will come and [D]wash them clear
[C]Still we know that [D]we were here
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Repeat chorus}
